import { JsonReaderCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> JsonReaderCopy = JsonReaderCopy {
  summary: "Use field to read a required name from a JSON object. It reports an absent field or checks a present value with the function you supply.",
  taskTitle: "Extract a required name from API data",
  purpose: "Display the string name in an object returned by an API. Unused fields such as active are fine. Return separate short explanations when name is missing and when it is not text.",
  typescriptBefore: "The TypeScript version stores JSON.parse's result as unknown and checks that it is a non-null, non-array object. Object.hasOwn checks for name, and typeof establishes that it is a string before display. There is no check rejecting the extra active field.",
  benefit: "field combines the object check, required-field lookup, and check of that value. The string check stays reusable as stringDecoder, and the caller receives either a checked name or a DecodeError.",
  setup: "json is the alias for std/json. The type annotation after the colon in let stringDecoder: json.Decoder<String> = decodeJson selects the string-reading version of decodeJson. Decoder<String> is a function receiving Json and returning Left with a failure reason or Right with a String.",
  after: [
    "With an existing Json value, json.field \"name\" stringDecoder value performs the lookup and check. Spaces separate the function and its arguments. The example leaves off that final value and stores json.field \"name\" stringDecoder as the reusable nameDecoder function.",
    "fn report source: String -> String is an ordinary function: the colon gives the parameter type and -> gives the return type. Its first match distinguishes parse's Left failure from its Right parsed Json. The underscore in Left _ ignores the detailed reason.",
    "It then calls nameDecoder value. Right name produces Name: Mio. For Left error, another match inspects error.kind: MissingJsonField produces Name is missing, and the remaining _ branch produces Name must be text. The first input's active field does not prevent extracting the name.",
    "main's do runs println calls in order, and _ <- discards each earlier print result before continuing. Unit means there is no useful return value; effect and with Console fails ConsoleError declare console access and possible printing failure. nameDecoder itself is an ordinary function.",
  ],
  details: [
    "field reads the selected field while allowing other fields in the input. To restrict an object to a declared field set, use record or a named struct with deriving JsonDecode.",
    "When name is absent, the reason is MissingJsonField and the error path ends at the parent object. When name exists but its string check fails, name is added to the path. Not every failure therefore has a path ending in name.",
    "An empty string is still a String and is accepted. This stringDecoder rejects null and false. If your application requires at least one character, add that check after reading the string.",
  ],
}
